  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Three teams – win the ball back at once",
  "description": "Split the group into three equal teams, for example three teams of three. Mark out a box of about 30 × 25 metres with cones in the middle of the ice. Two of the teams play together (blue) and keep the ball against the third (red) inside the box.\n\nWhen red win the ball the roles flip at once: red try to keep it for as long as they can and blue must win it back within a few seconds. Count how many passes red manage. Change which team is on its own after one minute, and play rounds of about three minutes with easy skating in between.\n\nVariation: put two cone goals outside the short sides of the box. If red win the ball they score by skating it through one of the cone goals, and blue may then leave the box and skate back to protect them. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The nearest player skates straight at the ball carrier when the ball is lost – think three seconds."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The others close the short passes so the pressed player cannot play out."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "If you are beaten: skate back on the right side, between the ball and the goal you protect."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "With the ball: make the box big and keep your stick and body facing the open ice."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "warmup",
  "difficulty": 2,
